---
import AppLayout from '../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { getMessages, localePath } from '../../i18n';
import AgentToSeedBridge from '../../components/AgentToSeedBridge.astro';
const m = getMessages('en');
---
<AppLayout title={m.guide.pageTitle} description="Understand Agent, SEED, and OpenEvo runtime/training mechanisms, then enter the current WebShop experiment and reproduction guide." locale="en">
  <div class="shell editorial-page guide-learning-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-kicker">Learning guide</span>
      <h1>Agent, SEED, and OpenEvo</h1>
      <p class="lede">Start from multi-step agent runtime, understand SEED parameter learning and OpenEvo cross-task evolution, then enter the current WebShop experiment.</p>
    </header>

    <AgentToSeedBridge locale="en" />

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="seed-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Paper method</span><h2 id="seed-guide-title">SEED reproduction reference</h2></div></div>
      <p>The SEED paper uses Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct, ALFWorld, and WebShop, with hindsight-skill SFT, on-policy rollout, GRPO, and OPD. Strict reproduction should pin the paper model, task protocol, and training definition first.</p>
      <div class="guide-cards">
        <a href={localePath('en','/papers/seed/')}><strong>SEED paper</strong><span>Paper conditions, model roles, training stages, and reproduction material</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/seed/')}><strong>SEED method</strong><span>Hindsight skills, OPD, GRPO, and parameter updates</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/benchmarks/')}><strong>ALFWorld / WebShop</strong><span>Tasks, actions, scoring, and failure evidence</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="openevo-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Current experiment</span><h2 id="openevo-guide-title">OpenEvo × WebShop</h2></div></div>
      <p>The active line has moved beyond RTX6 (4×RTX3090). Formal experiments are maintained in <code>openevo-experiment</code>, with a current allocation of <strong>5×RTX5090</strong>; Phase G is complete and Phase H0 Natural Success Search is next.</p>
      <div class="guide-cards">
        <a href={localePath('en','/guide/openevo-webshop-alfworld/')}><strong>Reproduction guide</strong><span>Current topology, experiment identity, WebShop records, and Phase H0</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/experiment/')}><strong>Experiment entry</strong><span>WebShop task data flow and current experiment phase</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/results/')}><strong>Experiment results</strong><span>Phase D–F, Phase G, historical repositories, and next steps</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="history-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">History</span><h2 id="history-guide-title">RTX6 and retired repositories</h2></div></div>
      <p><code>seed3090</code> and <code>openevo-webshop</code> remain provenance sources for 4×RTX3090 engineering, WebShop bring-up, failure traces, and early SD-LoRA diagnostics, but they are no longer current experiment entry points.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</AppLayout>

<style>
  .guide-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem}.guide-cards a{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.guide-cards strong,.guide-cards span{display:block}.guide-cards span{margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.76rem;line-height:1.45}.section>p{max-width:78ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}@media(max-width:720px){.guide-cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
